                                                    "text": "================================================================================\nyoi_cascade_formants — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA vowel filter built like a vocal tract: five two-pole formant resonators\nin series (an all-pole cascade), each at unity gain below its formant.\nUnlike the parallel version, the tuba's low end passes untouched and the\nupper formants fall off naturally, so it sounds like the tuba is singing\nthrough a mouth rather than through three bandpasses. in3 glides the vowel\nU -> O -> I.\n\nSource: Cook, DAFx-98 COO62 (formants as vocal-tract tube modes, all-pole\nformant filtering); Traube & D'Alessandro, DAFx-05 P_104 §1.5 (vowels in\nthe (F1, F2) plane).\n\nPARAMETERS (3)\n\n1. formant_shift_st — -12…+12 semitones, default 0\n   Moves all five formants together without changing the vowel: down =\n   bigger, darker mouth; up = smaller, brighter.\n\n2. freq_offset_st — -36…+36 semitones, default 0\n   Offsets the vowel position that arrives on in3. 24 st moves from U to\n   O, 48 st from U to I.\n\n3. width — 0…100 %, default 50 %\n   Adds a side signal from a copy with its formants shifted up to +1 octave\n   (at 100 %). L+R is exactly the plain filter, so mono is unaffected.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo audio.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3: vowel position as a frequency in Hz, log scale: 200 Hz or lower =\n  U, 800 Hz = O, 3200 Hz or higher = I. Values <= 1 Hz are ignored (last\n  value held, 800 Hz = O at start).\n- in4: resonance 0…1 = formant Q 2…30 (log taper).\n\nNOTES\n- Formants (Hz): U 300 / 870 / 2240, O 570 / 840 / 2410, I 270 / 2290 /\n  3010 (log-interpolated), with F4 3300 and F5 3750 fixed. All five shift\n  with formant_shift_st.\n- Gain staging: output × 0.7 × (Q/2)^-0.4. With the test tuba, resonance 0\n  to 1 changes the level by between +1.3 dB (U, mono) and -4 dB.\n- Ringing formants give a high crest factor: expect peaks about 20 dB\n  above the RMS.\n- in3 / in4 are smoothed over 5 ms.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                                }
                                            }
                                        ],
