                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                                    "linecount": 46,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 907.0 ],
                                                    "text": "================================================================================\nlp_pole_mixing_ota — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA 4-stage OTA one-pole cascade with resonance feedback, Xpander style: the\noutputs of the five points along the cascade are mixed to give 24 dB\nlowpass, 12 dB lowpass, 12 dB bandpass or 12 dB highpass, all with the same\nresonance. One knob sweeps through them. The input stage saturates softly.\n\nSource: Trausmuth & Huovilainen, DAFx-05 P_293 (pole mixing of ladder stage\noutputs); Huovilainen, DAFx-04 P_061 §3–5 (input-stage saturation,\nfeedback up to 4); McClellan, DAFx-26 paper 28 (time-varying stability).\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. shape — 0…1, default 0\n   Response: 0 = LP4, 0.33 = LP2, 0.67 = BP2, 1 = HP2, crossfading in\n   between. Note that tuba has little energy up high, so the BP/HP end is\n   much quieter at high cutoffs. That is the filter working, not a level\n   bug.\n\n2. drive_db — 0…24 dB, default 3 dB\n   Saturation at the cascade input. Small-signal gain stays at unity.\n\n3. freq_offset_st — -36…+36 semitones, default 0\n   Transposes the cutoff that arrives on in3.\n\n4. width — 0…100 %, default 50 %\n   Adds a side signal from a copy of the filter tuned up to +1 octave (at\n   100 %). L+R is exactly the plain filter, so mono is unaffected.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo audio.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3: cutoff in Hz. Values <= 1 Hz are ignored (last value held, 600 Hz at\n  start).\n- in4: resonance 0…1 (feedback k = 4 × in4, 1 = edge of self-oscillation).\n\nNOTES\n- Gain staging: feedback cuts the lowpass passband by up to 14 dB. LP4 gets\n  half of that back (sqrt(1 + k)), LP2 a quarter (its tap already rings\n  6 dB more), BP/HP none. With the test tuba, resonance 0 to 1 raises the\n  level by at most ~5 dB (LP4 with cutoff at 150 Hz) and lowers it at high\n  cutoffs.\n- in3 / in4 are smoothed over 5 ms.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                                }
                                            }
                                        ],
