                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                                    "linecount": 48,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 946.0 ],
                                                    "text": "================================================================================\ncomb_tanh_scream — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA feedback comb with a tanh saturator inside the loop. At moderate\nresonance it rings like a comb that gets grittier the longer it rings. Past\n~0.93 the loop gain goes above 1 and it self-oscillates: a screaming,\npitched drone locked to in3. The saturator keeps that drone bounded.\n\nSource: Chowdhury, DAFx-20 paper 3 §2.2 and §4 (saturating nonlinearity in\nthe feedback path keeps a recursive filter bounded); Norilo, DAFx-14 §3\n(combs with nonlinear feedback as modulation-delay effects).\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. polarity — -1…+1, default +1\n   +1 = positive feedback, peaks at f, 2f, 3f… (bright, buzzy).\n   -1 = negative feedback over half the period, peaks at f, 3f, 5f… (hollow,\n   square-ish, same pitch). Toward 0 the feedback (and the resonance) fades.\n\n2. drive_db — 0…24 dB, default 12 dB\n   Saturation inside the loop. More drive = the ring distorts sooner and\n   the self-oscillation is quieter and grittier. At 0 dB the scream is\n   loudest and cleanest.\n\n3. freq_offset_st — -36…+36 semitones, default 0\n   Transposes the comb pitch that arrives on in3.\n\n4. width — 0…100 %, default 50 %\n   Adds a side signal from a second comb tuned up to +1 octave (at 100 %).\n   L+R is exactly the plain comb, so mono is unaffected.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo audio.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3: comb pitch in Hz (sr/9990…sr/8). Values <= 1 Hz are ignored (last\n  value held, 600 Hz at start).\n- in4: resonance 0…1 = loop gain 0…1.08 (self-oscillates above ~0.93). It\n  keeps droning after the tuba stops until in4 comes down.\n\nNOTES\n- Gain staging: the tanh caps the feedback, so the makeup is gentler than\n  a plain comb's: (1 - cm)^0.3 (1 + cm)^0.25 with cm = min(|loop gain|,\n  0.95). With the test tuba, resonance 0 to 1 stays between about +7 dB\n  (drive 0, comb on the tuba's pitch, mono) and -9 dB.\n- A fixed 6 kHz lowpass in the loop takes the fizz off the scream.\n- in3 / in4 are smoothed over 5 ms.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                                }
                                            }
